ypically added with\n2237 |                 ``set_table_attributes``.\n2238 |               - \"table_styles\": CSS selectors and properties, typically added with\n2239 |                 ``set_table_styles``.\n2240 |               - \"hide_index\":  whether the index is hidden, typically added with\n2241 |                 ``hide_index``, or a boolean list for hidden levels.\n2242 |               - \"hide_columns\": whether column headers are hidden, typically added with\n2243 |                 ``hide_columns``, or a boolean list for hidden levels.\n2244 |               - \"hide_index_names\": whether index names are hidden.\n2245 |               - \"hide_column_names\": whether column header names are hidden.\n2246 |               - \"css\": the css class names used.\n2247 | \n2248 |         Returns\n2249 |         -------\n2250 |         Styler\n2251 |             Instance of class with defined styler attributes added.\n2252 | \n2253 |         See Also\n2254 |         --------\n2255 |         Styler.export : Export the non data dependent attributes to the current Styler.\n2256 | \n2257 |         Examples\n2258 |         --------\n2259 | \n2260 |         >>> styler = pd.DataFrame([[1, 2], [3, 4]]).style\n2261 |         >>> styler2 = pd.DataFrame([[9, 9, 9]]).style\n2262 |         >>> styler.hide(axis=0).highlight_max(axis=1)  # doctest: +SKIP\n2263 |         >>> export = styler.export()\n2264 |         >>> styler2.use(export)  # doctest: +SKIP\n2265 |         \"\"\"\n2266 |         self._todo.extend(styles.get(\"apply\", []))\n2267 |         table_attributes: str = self.table_attributes or \"\"\n2268 |         obj_table_atts: str = (\n2269 |             \"\"\n2270 |             if styles.get(\"table_attributes\") is None\n2271 |             else str(styles.get(\"table_attributes\"))\n2272 |         )\n2273 |         self.set_table_attributes((table_attributes + \" \" + obj_table_atts).strip())\n2274 |         if styles.get(\"table_styles\"):\n2275 |             self