3 | colors = mpl.colormaps['Dark2'].colors\n44 | \n45 | fig, ax = plt.subplots(layout='constrained')\n46 | \n47 | for i, color in enumerate(colors):\n48 |     ax.plot([0, i], color=color)\n49 | \n50 | plt.show()\n51 | \n52 | # %%\n53 | # See Also\n54 | # --------\n55 | #\n56 | # For more details about manipulating colormaps, see :ref:`colormap-manipulation`.  To\n57 | # change the default color cycle, see :ref:`color_cycle`.\n58 | #\n59 | # .. admonition:: References\n60 | #\n61 | #    The use of the following functions, methods, classes and modules is shown\n62 | #    in this example:\n63 | #\n64 | #    - `matplotlib.colors.Colormap`\n65 | #    - `matplotlib.colors.Colormap.resampled`\n66 | #\n67 | # .. tags::\n68 | #\n69 | #    component: colormap\n70 | #    styling: color\n71 | #    plot-type: line\n72 | #    level: intermediate\n73 | \n```\n\nFound class `lib/matplotlib/colorizer.py:Colorizer`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nJust show the structure of this class due to response length limitations:\n```\nclass Colorizer:\n    def __init__(self, cmap=None, norm=None):\n...\n    def _scale_norm(self, norm, vmin, vmax, A):\n...\n    @property\n    def norm(self):\n...\n    @norm.setter\n    def norm(self, norm):\n...\n    def to_rgba(self, x, alpha=None, bytes=False, norm=True):\n...\n    @staticmethod\n    def _pass_image_data(x, alpha=None, bytes=False, norm=True):\n...\n    def autoscale(self, A):\n...\n    def autoscale_None(self, A):\n...\n    def _set_cmap(self, cmap):\n...\n    @property\n    def cmap(self):\n...\n    @cmap.setter\n    def cmap(self, cmap):\n...\n    def set_clim(self, vmin=None, vmax=None):\n...\n    def get_clim(self):\n...\n    def changed(self):\n...\n    @property\n    def vmin(self):\n...\n    @vmin.setter\n    def vmin(self, vmin):\n...\n    @property\n    def vmax(self):\n...\n    @vmax.setter\n    def vmax(self, vmax):\n...\n    @property\n    def clip(self):\n...\n    @clip.setter\n    def clip(self, clip):\